<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/543> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/48> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dative"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/776> ;
    skos:scopeNote "The dative case is a grammatical case used in some languages to indicate, among other uses, the noun to which something is given. Usually the dative marks what would be considered the indirect object of a verb. Sometimes the dative has functions unrelated to giving. In some languages, the term dative case is used in traditional grammars to refer to the prepositional case-marking of nouns following simple prepositions and the definite article."@en .

