<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/822> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1085> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kostümbild"@de,
        "Costume design"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2175>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2177> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Costume design is the art of designing and creating costumes for the characters acting onstage (theatre) or appearing on the screen (cinema etc.). Its semiotics constitutes a metalinguistic framing of the stage action and can designate a character, a specific period of time, a people, a social class, etc."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/833> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/491> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Boustrophedon script style"@en ;
