<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/30> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.dariah.eu/bbt/Concept/000005> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Epochs"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "This term classifies cultural, social, intellectual phenomena consistent with each other thus creating intelligible unities. These types of phenomena are spatially and temporally limited and their consistency relies on the appearance of at least one qualitative element that links them in a unity. The spatial and temporal restriction is a formal feature of the facet “types of epochs”. That means that the facet “types of epochs” has no reference to specific realizations of these types of phenomena. Consequently, this facet does not include time periods such as the Renaissance or the Roman period, or the period of the Balkan wars etc., but the types of their categorization<strong>, </strong>i.e. the abstract concepts by virtue of which it is possible to conceive the cultural, social and intellectual phenomena as coherent."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/316> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/31> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ethnography (method)"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/147>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/190>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/355>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/527> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Field-based research method that focuses on the detailed documentation and multifaceted approach of the social and cultural aspects of a social milieu, with an aim to identify the relationships, the structures and the meanings that permeate it.&nbsp;"@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/32> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.dariah.eu/bbt/Concept/000009> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Geopolitical units"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2625> ;
    skos:scopeNote "This hierarchy comprises types of administrative divisions used by a state or other sovereign or political structure within the boundaries of its jurisdiction. Intrinsic features of these units include, among others, the extent of the area over which they are applied/exercised, the chronological extent during which they are in force, their governing bodies and the degree of autonomy they are granted in relation to managing and exploiting of their resources."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> .

