        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/457> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Population groups, whose members have a similar position in respect to production processes and sociopolitical power relations, and share common interests. The concept of social class refers rather to societies that are characterized by institutional equality and a capitalistic market economy in the framework of modernity."@en .

