    skos:prefLabel "Main clauses"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/469> ;
    skos:scopeNote "A main clause must contain a subject and a verb as well as express a complete thought. A main clause is the essential component of syntax and of language. Without a main clause, a group of words is a fragment, a major error in writing and in speech acts."@en .

