        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/426>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/834> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Α distinctive recurrent theme, idea, image, pattern, character-type feature, unit of the plot or other element of artistic creation found in an autonomous work or in a series of works, such as musical compositions, literary and dramatic texts, works of art, movies etc."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/23> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Immobile objects (monuments)"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.dariah.eu/bbt/Concept/000018> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Built environment"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "This term classifies structures, simple or complex, regardless of their size, duration of construction or use, that are attached or embedded in the ground and cannot be moved without irreversible damage."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2360> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1445> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "International currency (antiquity)"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1444>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1798>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1829>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1877>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1889>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2361> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Gold, electrum and mainly silver coins, which circulated widely, that is beyond the limits of their issuing authority. Their acceptance was not imposed by their issuing authority, but rather was the result of their high commercial value."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2477> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2529> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pharmacology"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1602>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1603>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2377>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2422>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2467>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2476> ;
    skos:scopeNote "The study of the properties of drugs and their effects on living organisms. The knowledge of the action of drugs has been consolidated and systematised in a number of distinct learned traditions from the ancient world to modern pharmacology which is characterised by systematic experimental and clinical investigation for disease treatment."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2520> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2529> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Seismology"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1832>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1836>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2521>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2548>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2599>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2600> ;
    skos:scopeNote "The branch of geophysics that examines the behaviour and products of elastic (seismic) waves travelling within the earth, which are produced by earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, explosions (including nuclear explosions) and meteorite impacts. Seismology began to flourish as a separate field of inquiry in the second half of the 19th century in conjuction with earthquake studies and the development of precise seismographs. The discipline covers documentation of events and effects (observations, maps, catalogs), instrumentation and analysis, theory and application, and it has been based on the international cooperation and standardization, already from the early 20th century."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2625> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2582> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Political science"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1114>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1229>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/32>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/44>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/475>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/520> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Academic discipline which is devoted to the systematic description, explanation, analysis and evaluation of politics and power. The major subfields of inquiry include political thought, political theory, political history, political institutions, comparative political analysis, public administration, public policy, rational choice, political sociology, international relations, and theories of the state."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2635> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/22>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/25> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Narrative text types"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1334>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/215>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2536> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Texts mainly in prose, either literary or historical and journalistic, such as the novel, the narration of historical events, the news report, the memoir, etc. These texts present in oral or written language a sequence of fictional or non-fictional events, or a combination of both. The succession of events is given by a narrator."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/29> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.dariah.eu/bbt/Concept/000019> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Physical features"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "This term classifies specific formations that are integrally adapted to certain material objects. They cannot, therefore, be separated from the carrier-object, but they also do not identify with it, since it is only a part of the carrier-object that carries the entire feature. In this sense, the feature is fixed, with respect to the carrier-object, while any attempt to remove it will result in the loss of part of the carrier-object. They may have two- or three-dimensional geometric extent, but there are no natural borders that separate them completely, in an objective way from the carrier-objects. Instances of Physical Features can be features in a narrower sense (scratches, holes, reliefs, surface colours etc.), while in the wider sense, they are portions of particular objects with borders that are not absolutely defined, such as the core of the Earth or the head of a marble statue."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/291> a skos:Concept ;
