        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/68> ;
    skos:scopeNote "The basic structure (Ego, parents/spouses and maternal brother) that corresponds conceptually to the principal organisational principles (consaguinity, affinity, descent) of kinship systems."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/542> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/215> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Narrator"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The subject, the narrating agent, who transfers a story verbally –orally or in writing– to someone else. The narrator does not exist in real life, but is part of the fictional world created by the author. The narrator is the method through which the author tells the story to the reader."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/569> a skos:Concept ;
