        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/88> ;
    skos:scopeNote "A noun is a part of speech that functions as the name of some specific thing or set of things, such as living creatures, objects, places, actions, qualities, states of existence, or ideas. Linguistically, a noun is a member of a large, open word group whose members can occur as the main word in the subject of a clause, the object of a verb, or the object of a preposition."@en .

