<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/14> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.dariah.eu/bbt/Concept/000015> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Natural disasters"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "This term classifies changes in states, things and entities that can be attributed to activity of natural phenomena and whose effect is such as to cause the dissolution or modification of the subject of these changes to the degree that their identity is destroyed."@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1467> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/31> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Weight standards"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1444>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1445> ;
    skos:scopeNote "The standardised weight systems according to which coin denominations were produced in various areas of the ancient Greek world. During the Archaic and the Classical period the main monetary standards of the Greek world were the Aeginetan, the Corinthian and the Euboeic, from which the Attic system derived."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/148> a skos:Concept ;
