    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1762>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1765> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Committees appointed by the Council by ordination or by drawing to offer their services. Their term of office lasted for a year or until the completion of the work assigned to them."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2582> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/248> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social sciences"@en ;
    skos:related <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1270>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1506>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1581>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2448>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2457>,
        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/2529> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Sciences that study social phenomena and relations, using a range of research methods (qualitative and quantitative), tools and approaches. They include the disciplines of economics, political sciences, sociology, social anthropology and ethnography; they claim law and psychology; and at their boundaries they meet with the fields of history (social history), biology (sociobiology), geography (social geography), philosophy (social philosophy), linguistics (sociolinguistics) etc. The idea of social sciences as a &quot;family&quot; of disciplines that focus on various aspects of human society&nbsp;emerged in the second half of the 19th century, following the example of empiricist methods of natural sciences."@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/289> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/26> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Occupational groups"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Occupational groups are sets of people who perform jobs whose main tasks and duties are characterized by a high degree of similarity. They may perform their jobs either for an employer or in self-employment.&nbsp;"@en .

