        <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/575> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Systems of religious faiths and practices that share the basic principles of Christianity, as they are presented in the Scriptures (Old and New Testament) and in Holy Tradition, but differ from each other in certain dogmatic issues, in the recognition of sacraments, and in the organization of the Church and the clergy.<br />"@en .

<https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/1659> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Rhetorical figures"@en ;
    skos:broader <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr/dyas-resource/Concept/31> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://humanitiesthesaurus.academyofathens.gr> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Figures of speech"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Figures of speech are ways of expression that deviate from literal statement or common usage of speech. They are specific expressive choices that emphasize, clarify, or embellish both written and spoken language. These speech patterns are related to: a) the grammatical agreement of the words; b) the position of the words in the sentence; c) the meaning of the words; d) the completeness of the speech.<br />&nbsp;"@en .

